-- AtlasDeChasse static data. Do not edit by hand.
-- Generated by tools/build-data.js on 2026-11-21 from tools/cache/petopia-abilities.html
-- (Petopia Forever abilities.php, fetched once), HunterPetJournal data (spell ids, families,
-- coordinates, uiMapID), the Polestar locale packs' NPC names (frFR, deDE, esES, esMX),
-- warcraft.wiki.gg (Zones by level (original) wikitext, cached 2026-11-21), for zone factions, and
-- Wowhead NPC pages (spawn points of the open-world teachers HunterPetJournal omits),
-- Wowhead's hunter-pets catalogue (beasts, levels, ranks and spawn points of the zones
-- HunterPetJournal does not carry at all, Mount Hyjal today).
--
-- Conventions:
--   src = "beast" when the ability is learned by taming a beast, "trainer" when a pet
--         trainer teaches it, "both" when both apply. On a beast, src names the source that
--         first carried it: "petopia", "hpj" or "wowhead" (its hunter-pets catalogue).
--   families = "all" for general abilities, else a list of family ids.
--   a beast's name in the client's language: fr is frFR, de is deDE, es is esES and mx is
--          esMX (the two Spanish clients name a share of the beasts differently, so both
--          ship; nil when Polestar has no name for that beast in that language).
--   family icon is the client texture name; it is nil for Fox and Core Hound, which have
--          no family icon, so fall back to iconId (always set) for those two.
--   a beast's family comes from HunterPetJournal (else Petopia's teacher line); the Wowhead
--          hunter-pets catalogue corrects it when the two disagree.
--   teachers = npc ids from ns.beasts, sorted by the level they can be tamed at.
--   zoneEn is the open world zone HunterPetJournal lists first, else the zone Wowhead's
--          hunter-pets catalogue names for the beast; nil for dungeon-only beasts (their
--          instance name is in dungeonZone).
--   spots are map/x/y points: one per zone from HunterPetJournal, plus up to three cluster
--          centres per zone from Wowhead (its NPC pages and its hunter-pets catalogue). A beast
--          can carry HunterPetJournal spots in one zone and Wowhead spots in another: the
--          catalogue only adds the maps a beast does not have yet.
--          spotsSrc = "wowhead" is set only when every spot of the beast comes from there, and
--          "ingame" when they all come from the maintainer's sightings in the SavedVariables;
--          a list mixing two sources has no spotsSrc.
--   verified = true when the maintainer tamed the beast and the pet it gave covers every rank
--          Petopia lists for it.
--   zone faction is "Alliance" or "Horde" from warcraft.wiki.gg's bar colours; nil for
--          contested and combat zones, and for zones the page does not list.
--   Faster Attack is built from ranks read off the live client only; its other ranks
--          and teachers are unknown, so its rank list is incomplete by design.
